        "original_id": "d083e81a-132f-5b17-b3da-b3202919450d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Martin Flavin, Peter Benchley, George Archainbaud, Beulah Marie Dix, Steven Spielberg\n- Works: Three Who Loved, Jaws, Jaws novel\n- Topics: American writers, film adaptations\n\nFacts:\n- Martin Flavin was born on November 2, 1883, and was an American playwright and novelist.\n- Three Who Loved is a 1931 American Pre-Code drama film directed by George Archainbaud.\n- Three Who Loved was written from a screenplay by Beulah Marie Dix based on a story by Pulitzer Prize-winning author Martin Flavin.\n- Peter Benchley was born on May 8, 1940, and was an American author and screenwriter.\n- Jaws is a 1975 American thriller film directed by Steven Spielberg.\n- Jaws was based on Peter Benchley’s 1974 novel of the same name.\n- Martin Flavin died on December 27, 1967.\n- Peter Benchley died on February 11, 2006.",
